{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q28209089","formula":"C₁₉H₂₉BrO₃","hill":"C19H29BrO3","elements":["H","C","O","Br"],"composition":{"C":19.0,"H":29.0,"O":3.0,"Br":1.0},"names":{"en":"BOMT"},"descriptions":{"en":"BOMT, also known by its developmental code name Ro 7-2340 and as 6α-bromo-4-oxa-17α-methyl-5α-dihydrotestosterone, is a synthetic steroidal antiandrogen which was first produced in 1970 and was never marketed for medical use. It is the 6α-brominated, 4-oxygenated, and 17α-methylated derivative of the androgen dihydrotestosterone (DHT). Along with benorterone, cyproterone (and its C17α acetate ester, cyproterone acetate), and flutamide, BOMT was among the earliest antiandrogens to be developed and extensively studied, although it is less well-documented in comparison to the others."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":159972,"mass":385.3,"charge":0,"smiles":"C[C@]12CCC(=O)O[C@@H]1[C@H](C[C@@H]3[C@@H]2CC[C@]4([C@H]3CC[C@]4(C)O)C)Br","inchikey":"ZUIGZKIOHUNINA-LWPUPYOYSA-N","iupac":"(1S,3aS,3bR,5S,5aS,9aR,9bS,11aS)-5-bromo-1-hydroxy-1,9a,11a-trimethyl-2,3,3a,3b,4,5,5a,8,9,9b,10,11-dodecahydroindeno[5,4-f]chromen-7-one","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"159972","atoms":52,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":2.651,"y":3.463,"z":-0.346,"el":"Br"},{"x":-5.209,"y":-0.839,"z":0.336,"el":"O"},{"x":3.819,"y":0.577,"z":0.148,"el":"O"},{"x":5.829,"y":-0.34,"z":-0.293,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.756,"y":-0.542,"z":0.203,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.934,"y":0.707,"z":-0.185,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.487,"y":0.655,"z":0.321,"el":"C"},{"x":0.212,"y":-0.606,"z":-0.28,"el":"C"},{"x":1.712,"y":-0.704,"z":0.164,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.164,"y":-0.137,"z":-0.335,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.087,"y":-1.765,"z":-0.449,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.609,"y":-1.899,"z":-0.036,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.819,"y":1.867,"z":0.257,"el":"C"},{"x":0.283,"y":1.933,